      "title": "Cash settlements on home insurance claims leaving vulnerable Australians short-changed, Asic says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/31/cash-settlements-home-insurance-cyclone-disaster-repairs-vulnerable-australians-asic",
      "description": "<p>Corporate regulator finds insurers settling most claims with cash rather than by managing repairs or rebuilding, warning of ‘unfair outcomes’ for homeowners</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Home insurers are overwhelmingly paying cash to settle claims, leaving Australians to foot blowouts in repair costs for their cyclone-damaged homes.</p><p>The corporate regulator is calling for “realistic” bigger payouts, warning the practice could cause “unfair outcomes” for people already in vulnerable positions.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/31/cash-settlements-home-insurance-cyclone-disaster-repairs-vulnerable-australians-asic\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-30T15:01:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Renee was at Gyirong Port minutes before flood struck, now her family want to travel from Australia to help search",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/renee-gyirong-port-flood-nepal-family-australia-help-search",
      "description": "<p>Missing woman’s partner and daughters fundraise to join search in one of the hardest-hit areas of Nepal </p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/30/nepal-tibet-floods-missing-australians-secret-harbour-byelection-wa-tanya-plibersek-insiders-pacific-islands-forum-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Clair Spry says her sister would hate the attention. She would want it focused on the Nepali people, who have been displaced or are in need of aid. She would want it to be on the impact of the climate crisis, especially on the world’s most economically vulnerable populations.</p><p>“Her focus right now would not be on her; it would be on the families,” Spry said. “So many people, the Nepalese people, that have been horribly displaced and traumatised. She would want the attention on them and how we are going to help them.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/renee-gyirong-port-flood-nepal-family-australia-help-search\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-30T06:21:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "One Nation’s Secret Harbour byelection win shows Labor is at a loss when it comes to calming angry voters | Analysis",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/30/one-nations-secret-harbour-byelection-win-shows-labor-is-at-a-loss-when-it-comes-to-calming-angry-voters",
      "description": "<p>Even after a week in which Pauline Hanson and One Nation candidates tripped over themselves trying to explain key policies, voters still backed the party</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The One Nation hype machine went into overdrive after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/30/one-nation-claims-victory-on-secret-harbour-byelection-in-western-australia\">Saturday’s Secret Harbour byelection</a> but one thing is clear from the thumping victory.</p><p>Despite the party’s sustained surge in public support, Labor and the Coalition still don’t have any idea how to calm an angry electorate and dint support for Pauline Hanson and her insurgent movement.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/30/one-nations-secret-harbour-byelection-win-shows-labor-is-at-a-loss-when-it-comes-to-calming-angry-voters\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-30T05:34:57"
    },
